course: dictionary
lesson: 7543
title: Predicting what happens next
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To predict something is to say what you think will happen before it happens. You make a good prediction by looking at clues and using what you already know. «Nobody can yet predict the exact day of an earthquake, but strong buildings save many lives.» So a prediction is not always possible, and it is not always right.
explain: In science, a prediction is a clear guess about what a test will show, made before you do the test. Then you test it and check your guess against the results. In a story, you can predict too: «Isla predicts the princess will save herself instead of waiting for a prince» uses clues from the story to guess what comes next, and she can check her guess as she reads on.
explain: A prediction is not a hope or a bad dream. «Nightmares are common in children, but they don't predict the future.» A good prediction is based on evidence, what you have seen and already know, not on fear or wishing.
fact: To predict means to say what you think will happen in the future, before it happens.
fact: In science, a prediction is what you expect a test to show, based on what you already know.
fact: Predict is a verb: predict, predicts, predicted, predicting.
fact: «Neptune was predicted by mathematics and found in 1846.»
fact: In 1862 Charles Darwin said a moth with a very long tongue must exist, and it was named «praedicta», meaning predicted.
exercise: «Nobody can yet predict the exact day of an earthquake.» What does predict mean here? | Wish for something good | Shake the ground | *Say what will happen before it happens | Measure something after it has happened
exercise: In science, Ravi says, «I predict the ice will melt faster in the sun.» What is he doing? | Pretending he knows nothing | Telling the result after the test | *Saying what he expects a test to show, before he tests it | Choosing a colour for the ice
exercise: «Nightmares don't predict the future.» What does this tell us? | Bad dreams always come true | Only adults have nightmares | *A bad dream cannot tell you what will really happen | Nightmares are a kind of weather forecast
test: Isla reads a story and says, «I predict the dragon will help the knight.» What is Isla doing? | Copying the ending from the back of the book | Remembering the story from last year | *Guessing what will happen next, using clues from the story | Drawing a dragon
test: Which job is about predicting the weather? | *Weather forecaster | Dentist | Baker | Bus driver
exam: Which of these is a correct use of predict? | Predict means to forget what happened yesterday | *Mathematics helped predict where Neptune was before anyone saw it | Nightmares always predict the future | Predict is a colour
